    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		mel, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to honey, honey-</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasa mellaria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 14, 49, § 82</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a bee-keeper,
				beemaster</i> (ante-class.), <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 17</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellārium</span></b> ,
			ii, n., <i>a beehive,
			apiary</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 12</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
